Era-split a role-reference Entity whose real-world referent changed
over time ("X's School" four years ago is not "X's School" today).
Closes the old node's era at split_date, mints a same-label successor
whose era opens there, mints the Disambiguation park point at the label
(future mentions attach there; the disambiguation scan re-points them by
evidence date), and chains old --succeeded_by--> successor. Edges named
in repoint_edge_ids move onto the successor (locked/duplicate edges are
skipped and reported).

Audited: requires a non-empty `reason`; refuses non-Entity nodes,
Disambiguation nodes, user-locked nodes, already-closed eras, and split
dates not after the node's start; snapshots into kg_revision_log. Pass
`dry_run: true` to preview without committing.
